                      <node index="0" text="The most useful technology often disappears into the background. It becomes a small part of an ordinary day: a conversation, an idea, a page you keep open.  Participation, without the ceremony  What if joining a network felt as natural as opening a browser tab? That is the promise worth exploring. A network grows stronger when participation fits the lives of the people using it.  Good tools make room for people. They make the complex parts manageable, while keeping the important choices visible.  The details matter: a clear label, a preserved draft, a place that remembers where you left off. These are the things that make an open system feel like home.  Build for the person using it, one thoughtful detail at a time.  An invitation to build  We do not need every answer today. We need a way to explore, to share what we learn, and to make the next step a little easier." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="nl.davidengelen.redsquare.dev" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" visible-to-user="true" bounds="[18,581][394,830]" drawing-order="0" hint="" display-id="0" />
